  "notes": [
    "Original game/source exports preserved; still images are optimized derivatives.",
    "Godot video clips are historical scripted-input gameplay captures.",
    "Unreal imagery shows development prototypes. Full missions, ordered keys, scoring and finale remain pending.",
    "The Eight Keys environment showcase uses current native v046 Jewel stills. The historical courtyard video and poster were removed from published assets on 28 October 2026; originals remain in project history.",
    "Encoding frame rates are not measured game performance. Full local source/receipt identities remain in ignored notes.",
    "Supplied artwork and branding retain their existing project rights. Font licenses are bundled in public/assets/fonts.",
    "Five-role badge images are 3D renders of actual exported STL meshes. No physical sample print or photograph of a printed badge has been verified.",
    "v031 native stills come only from selected versioned evidence captures. Role-lab, saved-map NPC review-camera and controlled-role contexts are identified separately. They do not verify physical controls, complete animation cycles or packaged Windows gameplay.",
    "Five v046 derivatives show the current native environment, unchanged Portal Hub character and actual menu. The menu backdrop is approved illustration shown inside native UI, not a gameplay render. No raw portrait, private new-head model, BIM source delivery or real-life visitor photograph is published.",
    "Eight v054 AI-generated mission concept sketches now lead the Eight Keys role tabs. They illustrate fictional proposed puzzles, not completed game scenes or verified construction details; native captures remain separately labelled in the gallery.",
    "28 October v055 adds the supplied upper-deck game screenshot and two clean native v046 upper-level views. These replace Eight Keys environment cover, story and gallery placements. Full frames and colours are preserved; no AI image alteration. The supplied screenshot retains its game HUD and has no independently verified scene version."
